Description: read "+" as a stress mark in Russian and Ukrainian text
 The PPA's sd_rhvoice marks the stress of Russian words with "+" (through
 liblinux-tts-text) when this is set; without it, only ё is added.
Author: Grigory Tuboltsev
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/config/RHVoice.conf	2026-11-23 16:53:07.910432628 +0100
+++ b/config/RHVoice.conf	2026-11-23 16:53:07.914138861 +0100
@@ -9,3 +9,8 @@
 ; Вы также можете скачать пример конфигурационного файла с комментариями по ссылке:
 ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RHVoice/RHVoice/master/doc/ru/RHVoice.conf
 ; и просто заменить им этот файл.
+
+; ppa:gtubolcev/linux-tts: "+" before a vowel marks the stress (Russian and
+; Ukrainian); speech-dispatcher's RHVoice module then gets the stress of
+; Russian words from the linux-tts stress dictionaries.
+stress_marker=+
